    "['vsi [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn vfi context v1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context v1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nl2vpn vfi context v1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nIn Cisco IOS, the equivalent command to create a Virtual Switch Instance (VSI) is `l2vpn vfi context [name]`, where:\\n- `l2vpn` enables Layer 2 VPN functionality\\n- `vfi` stands for Virtual Forwarding Instance\\n- `context [name]` creates a named VFI context, similar to HUAWEI's VSI\\n\\nThe Cisco command establishes the same basic container for Layer 2 VPN services as HUAWEI's `vsi v1` command.\", 'trans_template': 'l2vpn vfi context v1'}]]": 1,
    "['pwsignal bgp', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn vfi context v1', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context v1'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context v1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nl2vpn vfi context v1\\n autodiscovery bgp\\n  signaling bgp\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The `pwsignal bgp` command in Huawei configures BGP as the signaling protocol for the VPLS pseudowire in the VSI (Virtual Switching Instance).\\n2. The equivalent Cisco command uses:\\n   - `l2vpn vfi context v1` to enter VFI (Virtual Forwarding Instance) configuration mode (equivalent to Huawei's VSI)\\n   - `autodiscovery bgp` to enable BGP auto-discovery\\n   - `signaling bgp` to specify BGP as the signaling protocol\\n\\nNote that Cisco separates the auto-discovery and signaling components, while Huawei combines them under `pwsignal bgp`.\", 'trans_template': 'l2vpn vfi context v1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'autodiscovery bgp', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context v1'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context v1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nl2vpn vfi context v1\\n autodiscovery bgp\\n  signaling bgp\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The `pwsignal bgp` command in Huawei configures BGP as the signaling protocol for the VPLS pseudowire in the VSI (Virtual Switching Instance).\\n2. The equivalent Cisco command uses:\\n   - `l2vpn vfi context v1` to enter VFI (Virtual Forwarding Instance) configuration mode (equivalent to Huawei's VSI)\\n   - `autodiscovery bgp` to enable BGP auto-discovery\\n   - `signaling bgp` to specify BGP as the signaling protocol\\n\\nNote that Cisco separates the auto-discovery and signaling components, while Huawei combines them under `pwsignal bgp`.\", 'trans_template': 'autodiscovery bgp'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'signaling bgp', 'parent_command': ['l2vpn vfi context v1'], 'root': 'l2vpn vfi context v1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nl2vpn vfi context v1\\n autodiscovery bgp\\n  signaling bgp\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The `pwsignal bgp` command in Huawei configures BGP as the signaling protocol for the VPLS pseudowire in the VSI (Virtual Switching Instance).\\n2. The equivalent Cisco command uses:\\n   - `l2vpn vfi context v1` to enter VFI (Virtual Forwarding Instance) configuration mode (equivalent to Huawei's VSI)\\n   - `autodiscovery bgp` to enable BGP auto-discovery\\n   - `signaling bgp` to specify BGP as the signaling protocol\\n\\nNote that Cisco separates the auto-discovery and signaling components, while Huawei combines them under `pwsignal bgp`.\", 'trans_template': 'signaling bgp'}]]": 1,
