    "['tunnel-selector [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map s1 permit 10', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'address-family [address_family] vrf [vrf_name]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for `tunnel-selector s1`:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map s1 permit 10\\nmatch tunnel\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, `route-map` is used for similar purposes as Huawei's `tunnel-selector`\\n- The `permit` action and sequence number (10) match the Huawei configuration\\n- `match tunnel` is added because tunnel selection is involved\\n- Note that Cisco doesn't have an exact 1:1 equivalent to Huawei's tunnel selector concept, but this route-map configuration would be used in similar contexts where tunnel selection policies are applied in BGP/MPLS scenarios.\", 'trans_template': 'route-map s1 permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match tunnel', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'address-family [address_family] vrf [vrf_name]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Cisco command for `tunnel-selector s1`:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map s1 permit 10\\nmatch tunnel\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Cisco, `route-map` is used for similar purposes as Huawei's `tunnel-selector`\\n- The `permit` action and sequence number (10) match the Huawei configuration\\n- `match tunnel` is added because tunnel selection is involved\\n- Note that Cisco doesn't have an exact 1:1 equivalent to Huawei's tunnel selector concept, but this route-map configuration would be used in similar contexts where tunnel selection policies are applied in BGP/MPLS scenarios.\", 'trans_template': 'match tunnel'}]]": 1,
    "['signaling vpls', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'l2vpn signaling protocol bgp', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'address-family [address_family] vrf [vrf_name]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nl2vpn signaling protocol bgp\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `signaling vpls` command in the BGP L2VPN address family context enables VPLS signaling using BGP. The equivalent Cisco command is `l2vpn signaling protocol bgp`, which configures BGP as the signaling protocol for L2VPN services.\\n\\nNote: Cisco uses a different command structure where you must explicitly specify BGP as the signaling protocol for L2VPN/VPLS services, whereas Huawei's `signaling vpls` implies BGP signaling in this context.\", 'trans_template': 'l2vpn signaling protocol bgp'}]]": 1,
